    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0877" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">338.1121 Zrike Bros. and Johnson/9:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-07T21:00:00-05:00">April 7, 1933—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Reference Legation’s telegram No. 36 of April 5, noon.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d719-f1"/> Senator Hudicourt today introduced a resolution referring
                    to recent customs frauds which he estimated to total more than $200,000 and
                    called on the Government to “seize the occasion of these depredations” to insist
                    “through diplomatic channels” upon the return of the administration of Haitian
                    affairs and “especially the finances” to the Haitian people.</p>
                <p>Hudicourt supported by a small gallery of about 50 people asked for an immediate
                    vote on the resolution but the Senate wanted to refer it to committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
